/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 758 0 R
/E (Despite its advantages, technology poses challenges, particularly in terms of mental health. Excessive screen time and the pressure of curating perfect online personas lead to anxiety, loneliness, and low self-esteem. Social media can amplify comparisons, creating unrealistic standards. Additionally, the internet can be a breeding ground for misinformation, scams, and cyberbullying, putting vulnerable youth at risk. The rise of automation and AI also threatens traditional jobs, leaving young people uncertain about their futures. Navigating the digital world requires balancing opportunities with the need for privacy, mental well-being, and critical thinking in an ever-changing landscape.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
